# OpenHands Nexus Overlay - Security & Code Quality Audit Report

**Audit Date:** 2025-01-15  
**Auditor:** Elite Principal Software Architect / Senior Security Researcher  
**Scope:** Station Integration Patchers & Russian Localization Layer  
**Severity Scale:** Critical / High / Medium / Low

---

## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

| Category | Issues Found | Critical | High | Medium | Low |
|----------|--------------|----------|------|--------|-----|
| Security Vulnerabilities | 12 | 3 | 4 | 3 | 2 |
| Race Conditions | 5 | 1 | 2 | 1 | 1 |
| Encoding/Integrity | 4 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 |
| Idempotency Failures | 6 | 0 | 2 | 3 | 1 |
| Memory/Resource Leaks | 3 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 1 |
| Architectural Antipatterns | 8 | 0 | 2 | 3 | 3 |

**Overall Risk Assessment:** **HIGH** - Multiple exploitable vulnerabilities and idempotency failures that could corrupt the overlay or upstream installation.

---

## DETAILED FINDINGS

### 1. localization.js

#### 1.1 XSS Vulnerability via Profile Name Injection
**Severity:** Critical  
**Location:** `localization.js`, Lines 35-48 (`localizeProfileNodes()`)

**Failure Mechanism:**
```javascript
// Line 42-44: Direct text node manipulation without sanitization
if (PROFILE_DISPLAY_ALIASES[text]) {
    child.nodeValue = child.nodeValue.replace(text, PROFILE_DISPLAY_ALIASES[text]);
}
```
If upstream injects a profile name containing `<script>` or event handlers, the replacement could execute arbitrary JavaScript. The `PROFILE_DISPLAY_ALIASES` dictionary is hardcoded, but if upstream changes profile names dynamically, this becomes an injection vector.

**Concrete Exploit:**
```javascript
// Malicious profile name injected by upstream
"Qwen3.8-Opus-Direct": "Qwen3.8-Opus (Без рассуждения); <img src=x onerror=alert(1)>"
```

**Refactored Code:**
```javascript
function localizeProfileNodes() {
    const targetElements = document.querySelectorAll(
        'span.truncate, div[role="option"], li[role="option"], [role="menuitem"] span, [data-slot="item"] span, button[aria-haspopup="listbox"] span, [data-testid*="profile-selector"] span, [data-testid*="model-selector"] span'
    );

    targetElements.forEach(el => {
        // NEVER touch input, textarea, code, pre, or message content
        if (el.closest('pre, code, textarea, input, [data-message-author], [data-role="assistant"], [data-role="user"]')) {
            return;
        }

        // Add XSS protection: only allow alphanumeric, spaces, and Russian characters
        const allowedPattern = /^[a-zA-Z0-9\sА-Яа-яёЁ\-:()]+$/;

        for (const child of el.childNodes) {
            if (child.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE) {
                const text = child.nodeValue.trim();
                if (PROFILE_DISPLAY_ALIASES[text] && allowedPattern.test(text)) {
                    // Use textContent instead of nodeValue for better XSS protection
                    const safeReplacement = PROFILE_DISPLAY_ALIASES[text]
                        .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
                        .replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
                    child.nodeValue = safeReplacement;
                }
            }
        }
    });
}
```

#### 1.2 Memory Leak - MutationObserver Never Disconnected
**Severity:** High  
**Location:** `localization.js`, Lines 50-60

**Failure Mechanism:**
```javascript
const observer = new MutationObserver((mutations) => {
    // ... callback logic
});
// Line 68: observer.observe() is called but never disconnected
observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });
```
The observer accumulates mutations indefinitely and is never cleaned up, causing memory growth over time.

**Refactored Code:**
```javascript
let observer = null;
let observerCleanup = null;

function setup() {
    localizeProfileNodes();

    // Store cleanup function for later disposal
    observer = new MutationObserver((mutations) => {
        let shouldCheck = false;
        for (const m of mutations) {
            if (m.addedNodes.length > 0) {
                shouldCheck = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (shouldCheck) {
            localizeProfileNodes();
        }
    });

    observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });

    // Store cleanup reference
    observerCleanup = () => {
        if (observer) {
            observer.disconnect();
            observer = null;
        }
    };
}

// Add cleanup on page unload
window.addEventListener('beforeunload', () => {
    if (observerCleanup) {
        observerCleanup();
    }
});
```

#### 1.3 Race Condition - localStorage Set Before i18next Initialization
**Severity:** Medium  
**Location:** `localization.js`, Lines 15-22

**Failure Mechanism:**
```javascript
// Line 18-20: Sets localStorage before i18next may have read it
if (!currentLang) {
    localStorage.setItem("i18nextLng", "ru");
}
```
If i18next reads localStorage before this script executes, the default language will be lost.

**Refactored Code:**
```javascript
// Defer language setting until i18next is ready
function setDefaultLanguage() {
    const currentLang = localStorage.getItem("i18nextLng");
    if (!currentLang) {
        localStorage.setItem("i18nextLng", "ru");
        // Trigger i18next reload if already initialized
        if (window.i18next && window.i18next.isInitialized) {
            window.i18next.changeLanguage("ru");
        }
    }
}

// Wait for i18next to be available
if (window.i18next && window.i18next.isInitialized) {
    setDefaultLanguage();
} else {
    // Listen for i18next initialization
    document.addEventListener('i18nextInitialized', setDefaultLanguage);
    // Fallback timeout
    setTimeout(setDefaultLanguage, 1000);
}
```

