### 3. patch-agent-canvas-local-llm.ps1

#### 3.1 Hardcoded Model Names - Upstream Breakage
**Severity:** Medium  
**Location:** `patch-agent-canvas-local-llm.ps1`, Lines 25-30

**Failure Mechanism:**
```powershell
# Line 25: Hardcoded model name that could change
if ($content.Contains('llm_model:"openai/gpt-5.6-sol"')) {
    $content = $content.Replace('llm_model:"openai/gpt-5.6-sol"', 'llm_model:"openai/qwen"')
}
```
If upstream changes the default model name, this patch will fail silently.

**Refactored Code:**
```powershell
function Patch-DefaultModel {
    param([string]$Content, [string]$FilePath)

    # Use regex to find any model assignment, not hardcoded string
    $modelPattern = 'llm_model:\s*["\']([^"\']+)["\']'

    if ($Content -match $modelPattern) {
        $currentModel = $Matches[1]
        Write-Host "      Found current model: $currentModel in $($FilePath)" -ForegroundColor Gray

        # Only patch if it's the expected cloud model
        if ($currentModel -match 'gpt-.*|claude-.*') {
            $Content = $Content -replace $modelPattern, "llm_model:`"openai/qwen`""
            Write-Host "      Patched default model from $currentModel to openai/qwen" -ForegroundColor Green
        }
    }

    return $Content
}

# Usage:
foreach ($sf in $settingsFiles) {
    if ($sf.Name -like "*service*") { continue }
    $content = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($sf.FullName, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
    $content = Patch-DefaultModel -Content $content -FilePath $sf.FullName
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($sf.FullName, $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
}
```

#### 3.2 No Validation of Patch Success
**Severity:** Medium  
**Location:** `patch-agent-canvas-local-llm.ps1`, Lines 25-35

**Failure Mechanism:**
```powershell
# Line 25-30: No verification that patch was actually applied
if ($content.Contains('llm_model:"openai/gpt-5.6-sol"')) {
    $content = $content.Replace('llm_model:"openai/gpt-5.6-sol"', 'llm_model:"openai/qwen"')
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($sf.FullName, $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
}
```
If the file is read-only or write fails, the patch is silently skipped.

**Refactored Code:**
```powershell
function Test-PatchApplied {
    param([string]$FilePath, [string]$ExpectedContent)

    $content = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($FilePath, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
    return $content.Contains($ExpectedContent)
}

# Usage:
if ($content.Contains('llm_model:"openai/gpt-5.6-sol"')) {
    $content = $content.Replace('llm_model:"openai/gpt-5.6-sol"', 'llm_model:"openai/qwen"')
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($sf.FullName, $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)

    # Verify patch was applied
    if (-not (Test-PatchApplied -FilePath $sf.FullName -ExpectedContent 'llm_model:"openai/qwen"')) {
        Write-Error "Patch verification failed for: $($sf.FullName)"
        exit 1
    }
}
```

