### 6. common.ps1

#### 6.1 Secret Masking Incomplete
**Severity:** High  
**Location:** `common.ps1`, Lines 20-28

**Failure Mechanism:**
```powershell
# Line 20-25: Only masks certain patterns, could miss API keys in other formats
$clean = $msg -replace '[a-fA-F0-9]{48,64}', '[REDACTED_KEY]'
$clean = $clean -replace '(?i)(api[_-]?key\s*[:=]\s*["'']?)[^"''\s]+', '$1[REDACTED]'
```
API keys in different formats (base64, JWT, etc.) won't be masked.

**Refactored Code:**
```powershell
function Mask-Secrets([string]$msg) {
    if (-not $msg) { return "" }

    # Comprehensive secret masking patterns
    $patterns = @(
        # API keys (hex, base64, JWT)
        '[a-fA-F0-9]{48,64}',
        '[A-Za-z0-9+/]{40,}',
        'eyJ[a-zA-Z0-9_-]*\.eyJ[a-zA-Z0-9_-]*\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]*',

        # Common key patterns
        '(?i)(api[_-]?key\s*[:=]\s*["'']?)[^"''\s]+',
        '(?i)(token\s*[:=]\s*["'']?)[^"''\s]+',
        '(?i)(secret\s*[:=]\s*["'']?)[^"''\s]+',
        '(?i)(password\s*[:=]\s*["'']?)[^"''\s]+',

        # URLs with credentials
        '(?i)(https?://)[^@]+@',

        # AWS keys
        'AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}',

        # Private keys
        '-----BEGIN (RSA |EC |DSA |OPENSSH )?PRIVATE KEY-----'
    )

    $clean = $msg
    foreach ($pattern in $patterns) {
        $clean = $clean -replace $pattern, '[REDACTED]'
    }

    return $clean
}
```

#### 6.2 No Log Rotation
**Severity:** Medium  
**Location:** `common.ps1`, Lines 10-15

**Failure Mechanism:**
```powershell
# Line 10-15: Logs grow indefinitely
$Global:LogDir = Join-Path $Global:ProjectRootDir "Logs\Updater"
```
Log files will grow without bound, potentially filling disk space.

**Refactored Code:**
```powershell
function Rotate-Logs {
    param([string]$LogDir, [int]$MaxLogs = 10, [int]$MaxSizeMB = 100)

    if (-not (Test-Path $LogDir)) { return }

    # Remove old logs beyond limit
    $logs = Get-ChildItem -Path $LogDir -File | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending
    if ($logs.Count -gt $MaxLogs) {
        $logs[$MaxLogs..($logs.Count-1)] | Remove-Item -Force
    }

    # Compress large logs
    Get-ChildItem -Path $LogDir -File | Where-Object { $_.Length -gt ($MaxSizeMB * 1MB) } | ForEach-Object {
        $zipPath = "$($_.FullName).gz"
        Compress-Archive -Path $_.FullName -DestinationPath $zipPath -Force
        Remove-Item $_.FullName -Force
    }
}

# Call at start of each script
Rotate-Logs -LogDir $Global:LogDir
```

#### 6.3 Port Checking is Blocking
**Severity:** Medium  
**Location:** `common.ps1`, Lines 60-75

**Failure Mechanism:**
```powershell
# Line 60-75: Port check could hang indefinitely
function Test-ServicePort([int]$Port, [int]$TimeoutSec = 3, [int]$Retries = 5) {
    for ($attempt = 1; $attempt -le $Retries; attempt++) {
        try {
            $client = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient
            $iar = $client.BeginConnect("127.0.0.1", $Port, $null, $null)
            $wh = $iar.AsyncWaitHandle
            if ($wh.WaitOne($TimeoutSec * 1000, $false)) {
                $client.EndConnect($iar)
                $client.Close()
                return $true
            }
            $client.Close()
        } catch {}
```
If the port is in a zombie state, this could hang.

**Refactored Code:**
```powershell
function Test-ServicePort([int]$Port, [int]$TimeoutSec = 3, [int]$Retries = 5) {
    for ($attempt = 1; $attempt -le $Retries; $attempt++) {
        try {
            # Use timeout-aware connection
            $tcpClient = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient
            $connectTask = $tcpClient.ConnectAsync("127.0.0.1", $Port)

            if ($connectTask.Wait($TimeoutSec * 1000)) {
                $tcpClient.Close()
                return $true
            }
            $tcpClient.Close()
        } catch {
            # Continue to next retry
        }

        if ($attempt -lt $Retries) {
            Start-Sleep -Seconds 1
        }
    }
    return $false
}
```

